    },
    "body": "PR #1349's pinned lexical answer could change after its predecessor payload was evicted, and restored frames could substitute a permitted vocabulary token or skip the learned suffix. Read immutable identity metadata for the history feature and replay the bounded lexical policy during validation, including Stop/EOS and pre-capture counters. Keep learned parameters and the original exposed outputs unchanged.\n\nIndependent reconstruction confirms the four-word interface but finds incorrect temporal supervision, a clipped-count representation that cannot learn the proposed continuation, and preservation rows that bypass the realizer. Qualify those claims, reconcile resource records, and revise the next complete milestone to truthful evidence-conditioned lexical recurrence with source-separated text learning. The brief retains geometric reuse and gives DeepSeek substantive design discretion.\n\nValidation: 32 scoped-memory, 5 lexical-policy and 25 runner tests pass. The explicitly invoked saved-artifact test passes with 7 child processes and 62 parent +62 child complete-frame/effect comparisons, including actual predecessor/origin eviction. Independent verification checks all86 files of the sealed report. Formatting, claim wording and diff checks pass. Six artifact-dependent tests are ignored by default; no blanket suite claim. Original artifacts/failed attempts are preserved. Queue compatibility checks are not model validation. No model refit, new semantic acceptance, geometric-superiority or energy claim.\n\nReferences #820, #973, #1139, #962, #963, #964.\n",
